{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in the /workspace directory. I can see there are some existing directories (final_output, input_data, skill_context) and files (gen_inputs.py, setup.sh). I need to explore these to understand the existing structure and the raw market data that needs to be processed.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace to understand the existing structure. I'll check the input_data directory for raw_market_data.json, look at the skill_context folder for any guidance, and examine the setup.sh and gen_inputs.py files to understand how the system is intended to work.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la input_data/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input_data/raw_market_data.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found the raw market data for Electric Vehicles sector with 5 companies (AlphaMotors, BetaDrive, GammaCars, DeltaAuto, EpsilonEV). The data includes market share, revenue, YoY growth, total market size, forecast, key trends, and risks. I need to read the SKILL.md to understand the expected patterns for the agent system.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md file from skill_context to understand the expected agent structure and patterns. Then I'll create the 4 agent workspaces with their required files (SKILL.md, inbox/instructions.md, status.json) and outboxes for data flow between agents.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md output was truncated. I can see it's about agent orchestration with a specific workflow. I need to see the complete documentation to understand the agent generation and communication patterns.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file and check the references folder for sub-agent templates. This will help me understand the exact structure needed for each agent.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | tail -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is still being truncated. I need to see the full SKILL.md file content and check the references folder for templates.",
  "plan": "Use less or split the file reading to see the complete SKILL.md, and explore the references folder for sub-agent templates.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -100 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '100,200p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '200,300p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '300,400p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file is 175 lines total. I've seen lines 1-100 approximately. I need to see the rest (lines 100-175) to get the complete documentation, especially the references section for sub-agent templates.",
  "plan": "Read the remaining lines of SKILL.md (lines 100-175) and check the references folder for templates.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '100,175p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now understand the agent orchestration pattern from SKILL.md. The task requires 4 agents in sequence: data-collector → analyst → writer → reviewer. Each agent needs SKILL.md, inbox/instructions.md, status.json, and outbox/. The data-collector reads from input_data/raw_market_data.json and the final output goes to final_output/.",
  "plan": "Check the references folder for templates, then create the complete agent workspace structure with all required files for each of the 4 agents.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/communication-protocol.md 2>/dev/null || echo 'file not found'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/sub-agent-templates.md 2>/dev/null || echo 'file not found'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now have a clear understanding of the communication protocol. Each agent needs: SKILL.md, inbox/instructions.md, status.json, outbox/, and workspace/. The pipeline flows: data-collector → analyst → writer → reviewer. Let me read the sub-agent templates for more details.",
  "plan": "Read the sub-agent-templates.md file, then create all 4 agent workspaces with proper structure and files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/sub-agent-templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I now have all the information I need. The templates show the structure for each agent type. I need to create 4 agent workspaces: data-collector, analyst, writer, and reviewer. Each needs SKILL.md, inbox/instructions.md, status.json, outbox/, and workspace/. The pipeline flows sequentially: data-collector → analyst → writer → reviewer.",
  "plan": "Create the complete agent workspace structure. I'll start by creating the directories for all 4 agents, then create the SKILL.md, inbox/instructions.md, and status.json files for each agent.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p agents/data-collector/{inbox,outbox,workspace}\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p agents/analyst/{inbox,outbox,workspace}\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p agents/writer/{inbox,outbox,workspace}\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p agents/reviewer/{inbox,outbox,workspace}\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la agents/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
